{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 53, :comments ["<b>Et the live bird outside the city.</b> Rabbi Yosi the Galilean says: a bird that was outside every city — and which is this? The sparrow." "<b>And he shall atone for the house and it shall be purified.</b> If it is stated regarding the metzora — atonement — why is it stated regarding houses? And if it is stated regarding houses, why is it stated regarding the metzora? Because the metzora has purification by means of immersion and requires a sacrifice, unlike houses, for they are not capable of action; and in houses there are those that require removal, scraping, and plastering, unlike the metzora."], :book "leviticus", :voice :chizkuni, :lang :pt, :chapter 14, :timestamp "2026-07-30T20:19:38.134906310Z", :translated-from :en, :model "glm-5.2"}